course: dictionary
lesson: 7261
title: Meet the pika
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A pika is a small, round, furry mammal with short ears and no tail. It is related to rabbits, but it is a different animal. «Pikas are small round relatives of rabbits» tells you this, so you can picture a little rabbit-like animal.
explain: Pikas live among rocks on cold mountains in Asia and North America. The words «under rocks» and «warming mountains» in the example tell you where they make their homes.
explain: Pikas stack grass into «hay piles» under the rocks. They do this for winter, because they do not hibernate. Hibernating means sleeping through the cold months, so a pika must eat its stored grass instead.
explain: Pikas «overheat easily», so they need cool air. Warm weather is a danger to them. If you read the clues, you can work out why warming mountains are a problem for pikas.
fact: A pika is a small, round, furry mammal with short ears and no tail.
fact: Pikas are related to rabbits, but they are a different kind of animal.
fact: Pikas live among rocks on cold mountains in Asia and North America.
fact: Pikas collect grass into «haypiles» to eat in winter, because they do not hibernate.
fact: Pikas overheat easily, so warming mountains are a danger to them.
exercise: What kind of animal is a pika? | *A small, round, furry mammal with short ears and no tail | A insect that buzzes near flowers | A large bird that cannot fly | A fish that lives in rivers
exercise: The text says pikas are «relatives of rabbits». What does relatives mean here? | Enemies that fight over food | Rocks on a mountain | People who live in the same house | *Animals that are related to each other, like cousins
exercise: Where do pikas live, according to the lesson? | Deep under the sea | A hot desert with lots of sand | A warm beach by the sea | *Among rocks on cold mountains
test: Why do pikas stack grass into «hay piles»? | *To eat in winter, because they do not hibernate | To make a cosy bed for the summer | To decorate their rocks
test: Why are warming mountains a danger to pikas? | Because pikas can fly higher in the heat | *Because pikas overheat easily | Because pikas love hot weather | Because the rocks will float away
exam: Which clue shows that pikas need cool places to live? | *They «overheat easily», so warm mountains are dangerous | They are «small and round» | They are «relatives of rabbits» | They «stack grass into hay piles»
